+# iter_001-b2-a2 — skip the calibration-identity text decoder blocks, then INT4 the rest
+
+## What changed relative to the parent (`iter_001-b2-a1`)
+
+The parent keeps the exact structural removals (V-JEPA world model, tied `lm_head`,
+unused prompt-embedding rows) and INT4-packs every large Linear, reaching 79.6%
+memory reduction with 8/10 smoke successes.
+
+This node adds one structural change on top of that recipe:
+
+- **Skip text decoder layers 3–26.**  The frozen calibration's `block_influence`
+  reports the mean relative residual energy of each block on the calibration
+  states.  Text layers 3–26 all score between 5e-5 and 0.012 (layers 0, 1, 2, 27
+  score 1.25, 0.155, 1575 and 0.081), so those 24 blocks are effectively identity
+  on the frozen distribution.  They are replaced by an identity `SkipBlock`,
+  preserving layer indices and the DeepStack injection into layers 0–2.  This
+  removes ~1.2B text parameters instead of packing them.
+- Everything else follows the parent: compact embedding, action-position
+  compaction, and INT4 tinygemm weight-only quantization of the surviving text,
+  vision and action Linears.
+
+The intent is to trade a small, measured functional change for a large memory
+reduction, while keeping the same 8/10 smoke gate.
+
+## Last check output
+
+Pending: `python tools/check.py` has not been run yet for this node.
+
+## What I would try next
+
+If the action error stays small and smoke keeps 8/10, extend the same
+calibration-influence criterion to the low-influence vision blocks (12, 13,
+16–19) and action blocks (3–11, 13–15).  If the text skip breaks an episode,
+restore layers in reverse influence order (26, 25, …) until smoke recovers 8/10.
